- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vignette.html
- Summary (EN): Darkens the corners of an input layer, reducing brightness toward the edges to draw attention to the centre. Useful for framing a subject or giving an old lens look. Output: the vignetted layer.
- Résumé (FR) : Assombrit les coins d'une couche pour recentrer le regard, avec une forme ronde, rectangulaire ou mixte et un bord adouci.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the original layer to apply the vignetting to", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask whose amount is scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: sets the layer type the source accepts", "Mask: how much of the new value mixes with the original (default 1)", "Brightness: scales how bright or dim the vignette is", "Shape: Round (circular), Rectangle, or Blend between the two", "Circle Radius and Circle Scale: size of the round vignette and its non-uniform stretch", "Rectangle Size and Round Corners: size and corner rounding of the rectangle", "Blend: mixes Round and Rectangle when Shape is Blend", "Center: vignette centre in image space", "Blur: softens the edge of the vignette", "Shape Ramp: adjusts the shape profile of the vignette"]

- Caveats: ["The Shape Ramp only has a visible effect when the vignette is fairly smooth, meaning blurred"]

